218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Even with no clear answer as to how the system works, companies trust its effectiveness and efficiency and use it alongside human review. The system helps rank candidates so that interviewers can spend time reviewing just the top interviews rather than all interviews. HR gets to see how the candidates rank against skills crucial for the role being interviewed for. This saves a company time and money, allowing them to view interviews on their own time, rather than have scheduled ones for \(typically\) initial rounds of screening. However, there are still companies wary of the system due to the failures seen in other companies, such as the Intuit case discussed earlier.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
