313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Virtue ethics would call for a system that is fair, transparent, and just. Hirevue is more difficult to analyze in this perspective as there are many pros and cons. Starting with the cons, the system lacks empathy. In interviews, you are told to showcase your personality and emphasize how you fit the culture. However, candidates have expressed how talking to a screen really felt draining and dystopian. Furthermore, the system can be seen as unjust as it uses historical data that can perpetuate human biases. Lastly, the system is rather opaque as candidates view the algorithm as a black box. On the other hand, the pros of this system are it creates consistency with the same questions and process given to every candidate and the same objective metrics used to rate candidates. This creates a fair system that eliminates human assumptions in early rounds. Although the system is seen as a black box, Hirevue aims to be transparent and create an explainable system through its AI explainability statements. )
/E (Virtue ethics would call for a system that is fair, transparent, and just. Hirevue is more difficult to analyze in this perspective as there are many pros and cons. Starting with the cons, the system lacks empathy. In interviews, you are told to showcase your personality and emphasize how you fit the culture. However, candidates have expressed how talking to a screen really felt draining and dystopian. Furthermore, the system can be seen as unjust as it uses historical data that can perpetuate human biases. Lastly, the system is rather opaque as candidates view the algorithm as a black box. On the other hand, the pros of this system are it creates consistency with the same questions and process given to every candidate and the same objective metrics used to rate candidates. This creates a fair system that eliminates human assumptions in early rounds. Although the system is seen as a black box, Hirevue aims to be transparent and create an explainable system through its AI explainability statements. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [21 22]
>>
