330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The HR and legal teams would work together to redesign the candidate consent process to ensure true informed consent. Although Hirevue does reveal how its algorithms worked and what data is being collected, it fails to do so in a simple manner. Instead, candidates should be provided with a plain-language explanation of exactly what data is collected, how facial cues and environmental indicators are taken into consideration, and strides the company takes to mitigate harm from data breaches. Candidates should also be given the option to opt-out of this style and participate in video interviews without facial analysis or complete a structured phone interview. Many companies do provide a separate system to request accommodations, so this is extremely crucial. The Talent Acquisition Leads in HR should be trained on teaching hiring managers how to be accommodating without penalizing candidates opting out of biometric collection.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
