343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In conclusion, this assessment explored Hirevue, an AI-powered assessment platform used by HR to conduct and analyze video interviews and skill-based assessments. While Hirevue maintains extensive documentation that makes companies trust its use and allow it to replace rounds of screening, candidates are extremely skeptical of the system, claiming there is no transparent breakdown of how non-verbal cues are weighted. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [15 16]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (However, Hirevue is extremely promising. Aside from making the initial screening rounds less human, in a world where 200+ applications are expected prior to an offer, Hirevue is a means to meet demand in the troubling job market where HR is already overwhelmed with tasks and applicants.  The main ethical concerns were pertaining to algorithmic bias, the black box model, and privacy and data security. To address these concerns, the recommendations are to minimize collection of biometric data with automatic deletion, provide true informed consent process with opt-out options, mandate human oversight at all steps with the final decision made by humans, establish historical bias audits and diverse data requirements, and require Hirevue to provide algorithmic transparency prior working with this company. From an efficiency standpoint, Hirevue can add great value to the company. With the added recommendations, it would serve as a well-rounded system that improves efficiency that still maintains human-ness in the interview process.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [17 18]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (HR handles high-impact decisions with hiring, promotions, and performance evaluations. Maintaining ethical AI is crucial to ensure fairness, transparency, and accountability. Without safeguards to reduce bias, AI systems can create discriminatory results that lead to legal, financial, and reputational risks. It is our responsibility to ensure the AI systems we are using uphold organizational values, especially in an era where regulatory safeguards are being destroyed. We must hold ourselves accountable to ethical standards to protect all stakeholders.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [19 20]
>>
endobj
